cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TLHdig-TF: a Text-Fabric conversion of the Thesaurus Linguarum Hethaeorum digitalis"
message: >-
  Cite the source dataset, not this conversion, for any Hittitological claim.
  Cite this repository only when the conversion itself is what you are discussing.
type: software
version: "0.3.0"
authors:
  - family-names: Sosnovshchenko
    given-names: Oleksandr
repository-code: "https://github.com/alexsosn/TLHdig-TF"
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/alexsosn/TLHdig-TF/blob/main/LICENSE"
abstract: >-
  Converter and Text-Fabric dataset for TLHdig, the largest digital corpus of Hittite
  cuneiform transliterations. The code is MIT; the corpus under corpus/ and the
  generated dataset under tf/ are CC-BY-4.0, inherited from the source dataset, which
  must be attributed. The current tf/0.3.0 build is an integration prototype and is not
  suitable for research conclusions -- see KNOWN-ISSUES.md.
keywords:
  - Hittite
  - cuneiform
  - Text-Fabric
  - Assyriology
  - digital philology
references:
  - type: dataset
    title: "Thesaurus Linguarum Hethaeorum digitalis (TLHdig) Beta Version 0.3"
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.20328284
    year: 2026
    license: CC-BY-4.0
    url: "https://www.hethport.uni-wuerzburg.de/TLHdig/"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Müller"
        given-names: Gerfrid
      - family-names: Prechel
        given-names: Doris
      - family-names: Rieken
        given-names: Elisabeth
      - family-names: Schwemer
        given-names: Daniel
